    |
  7 |     sizes: [String:Int]{"z": 0, loop w in words -> w: 1}
    |                                 ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
 Why: A typed head holds either its items or one loop that builds them, so a reader sees at once what makes the collection
 Fix: Build the items and the loop's collection apart, then join them, such as `[0].concat(loop x in xs -> x)`
